LICENCE FOR COMPILED MAP DATA
=============================

This file covers the compiled map artifacts distributed with Heat Street. It does
not cover the game's source code, which is licensed separately.

See docs/adr/0001-map-data-source.md for the decision record this file implements,
including the source licences, the required attribution strings and the open legal
question this file exists to close.


1. Compiled road graphs (`*.map.json`) — ODbL v1.0
--------------------------------------------------

All compiled road-graph artifacts distributed with this project — every file
matching `*.map.json`, conforming to `docs/schemas/road-graph.v1.md` — are
licensed under the:

    Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0
    https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

These artifacts are derived from OpenStreetMap data, which is itself licensed
under ODbL v1.0 (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright).

Why ODbL and not "attribution only": ODbL distinguishes a Produced Work
(attribution only) from a Derivative Database (must itself be released under
ODbL). A `.map.json` road graph is a structured, machine-readable extraction of
OpenStreetMap ways and nodes, and is plausibly a Derivative Database. Rather
than leave that ambiguity open, this project takes the free safe path and
licenses these artifacts under ODbL v1.0 unconditionally. The project is then
compliant under either reading. This is recorded as Open Question 1 in
docs/adr/0001-map-data-source.md — unresolved in law, but mitigated in practice.


2. Compiled geometry (`*.glb`) — Produced Work, attribution only
----------------------------------------------------------------

Compiled map geometry (road ribbons, terrain meshes and other `.glb` artifacts
generated from the road graph and the elevation model) is treated as an ODbL
Produced Work. It requires attribution but is not itself released under ODbL.


3. Required attribution
-----------------------

Any distribution of this game or of the artifacts above must credit
OpenStreetMap. The following forms are acceptable:

    (c) OpenStreetMap contributors
    (c) OpenStreetMap

together with the licence URL, which must be included where linking is not
possible:

    https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

For games, the OpenStreetMap Foundation's attribution guidelines permit this
credit to appear on the credits page, in the menu, or in another suitable
location.

Where elevation data is sourced from Copernicus DEM GLO-30, its mandatory notice
must also be reproduced verbatim. The exact strings are recorded in
docs/adr/0001-map-data-source.md. USGS 3DEP is public domain and carries no
mandatory notice.

In this project the credit strings are not hand-maintained: they are carried in
the mandatory `attribution` block of every compiled `*.map.json` and rendered
onto the credits screen from the data itself.


4. Prohibited sources
---------------------

No bytes derived from Google Maps, Google Earth or Google Street View may enter
these artifacts, including geometry traced from such imagery. See
docs/adr/0001-map-data-source.md for the full statement and its citations.
